<title>EGYPT: Egypt cotton exports 49,953 tonnes so far - trade.</title>
<headline>Egypt cotton exports 49,953 tonnes so far - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt has exported 49,953 tonnes of cotton so far this season, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Exporters had sold 45,193 tonnes by November 16, the season's ninth week, Alcotexa said. The organisation coordinates prices and exports by private and state-owned firms.</p>
<p>It said exporters sold 4,760 tonnes between the ninth week of the marketing season and the 11th week, which ended on November 30.</p>
<p>Egypt has said that it expects to export 125,000 to 150,000 tonnes of this year's harvest. --Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
